From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:51:05 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] ps1-input

PlayStation games get all four shoulder buttons. owns_shoulders already
answers false for PS1, so L1 and R1 go to the game as on SNES and Mega
Drive, and a new owns_triggers policy with the same polarity answers false
for PS1 only: L2 and R2 then reach the core as libretro ids 12 and 13
instead of starting rewind and fast-forward. Every other system keeps the
rewind and fast-forward triggers.

Fast-forward moves to SELECT+R2, which turns it on with one press and off
with the next and never reaches the game, whichever button is let go
first; it is latched, so ejecting stops it. SELECT+X still flips the
picture, SELECT alone still reaches the game once the chord window closes,
and an L2 or R2 still held at eject is let go before the eject save. The
face buttons follow position: Cross on B, Circle on A, Square on Y and
Triangle on X, with turbo passing X and Y through.

Handing the triggers to the game follows gmaster1998/slot.ps1's toggle
(GPL-3.0).
